-e928-54f8-a113-98e22acbcee6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268227 #edb/ref 1080 "$u$ and $w$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268227 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268227 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9d91b88-d944-5bcf-aa2b-85fbc6643155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186267968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268407 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0274237b-5707-50b2-a56c-b7645a561434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186267669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268511 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3f7a808f-2559-583a-bc17-73f587979c51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268819 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ed26647f-f52c-560b-b302-af5032a00378" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269067 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269067 #edb/ref 1069 "q-135465" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269067 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269067 #edb/ref 1071 "A certain company produces three types of ground coffee: fine, medium, and coarse. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between the three types of ground coffee each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Fine** | **Medium** | **Coarse** |\n| To: | **Fine** | $0.5$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| **Medium** | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ |  |\n| **Coarse** | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |  |\n\nFor example, $30%$ of fine ground coffee customers switch to medium ground coffee each year, and $20%$ of coarse ground coffee customers switch to fine ground coffee.\n\nCurrently, $300\\,000$ customers buy fine ground coffee, $500\\,000$ customers buy medium ground coffee, and $200\\,000$ customers buy coarse ground coffee. How many customers will purchase fine ground coffee in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269067 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "25a6f23d-99a0-510e-abf4-afb5461a1de7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269067 #edb/ref 1074 "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of ground coffee is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}300\\,000 \\\\ 500\\,000 \\\\ 200\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}300\\,000 \\\\ 500\\,000 \\\\ 200\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 \\\\ 0.5 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.6 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 \\\\ 0.5 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.29 \\\\ 0.47 \\\\ 0.24\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $29%$ of customers will buy fine ground coffee. Computing $29%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.29=290\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $290\\,000$ customers will buy fine ground coffee in one year." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186269072 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269072 #edb/ref 1069 "q-135485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269072 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269072 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=\\begin{bmatrix}-0.2 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}0.15 \\\\ 0.95\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186269072 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11a06254-1131-54e3-ac79-433bb7764638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269072 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.15+0.95=1.1\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269084 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269084 #edb/ref 1069 "q-135566" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269084 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269084 #edb/ref 1071 "There are three cable TV providers in a particular apartment block: provider $A,$ provider $B,$ and provider $C.$ A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & a & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & b \\\\ c & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186269084 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40ee85ea-08ea-5955-8652-e4607e79ae86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269084 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C.$  This implies that $10%$ of them continue using provider $A.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue using provider $B.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$ This implies that $20%$ of them continue using provider $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Provider A** | **Provider B** | **Provider C** |\n| To: | **Provider A** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Provider B** | $0.8$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |  |\n| **Provider C** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & 0.25 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.1+0.1=0.45.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186322063 #edb/ref 1080 "520\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322063 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322063 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "758ee170-1fcb-5640-8b61-f22fb7a21811" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322316 #edb/ref 1080 "400\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322316 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322316 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "936daf2f-be59-5538-b600-77f0341e8b82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322665 #edb/ref 1080 "430\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322665 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322665 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3c760ab-015f-5f08-8419-73f7e6627df3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322760 #edb/ref 1080 "480\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322760 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322760 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ce8548e7-cae1-5bab-a94c-045833d4e0f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323073 #edb/ref 1080 "640\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323073 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323073 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f5b6826a-9e7d-507c-8455-dfd824432ed5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186323073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186322760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323663 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fe25491b-be23-5337-9805-76ec9cd44496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378664 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378664 #edb/ref 1069 "q-135457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378664 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378664 #edb/ref 1071 "A certain company produces two types of footwear: casual and sports. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between both types of footwear each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Casual** | **Sports** |\n| To: | **Casual** | $0.55$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Sports** | $0.45$ | $0.3$ |  |\n\nThat is, $45%$ of casual customers switch to sports each year, and $70%$ of sports customers change to casual.\n\nCurrently, $700\\,000$ customers purchase casual footwear, while $300\\,000$ customers purchase sports footwear. How many customers will purchase sports footwear in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378664 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "960aa206-ef2f-590f-b6e6-46bfb1026352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378664 #edb/ref 1074 "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.55 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.45 & 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of footwear is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}700\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}700\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.55 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.45 & 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.595 \\\\ 0.405\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $40.5%$ of customers will purchase sports footwear. Computing $40.5%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.405=405\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $405\\,000$ customers will purchase sports footwear in one year." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378665 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c01d1ab0-b4e0-570d-9f6a-3444da987d66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378666 #edb/ref 1080 "405\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378666 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378666 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1df1090c-b953-55e7-82db-2918444fb6f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378667 #edb/ref 1080 "425\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378667 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378667 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ddc961d6-6767-5034-8c94-13fc400c4870" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378668 #edb/ref 1080 "395\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378668 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 1